o about 3 seconds if the V)37(isual Memory battery is depleted. It\325)74(s )]TJT*(important to remember that an application cannot determine whether a controller has been dis-)TjT*-0.039 Tw(connected or whether a VMU has been inserted, so your caution message should not make the user )TjT*0 Tw(think that a controller has malfunctioned when the real situation is that a memory card has been )TjT*[(inserted. \(It isn\325)37(t necessary to display a warning when a VMU is removed, because removal of a )]TJET90 337.303 m539.668 337.303 lSBT10 0 0 10 116.689 342.652 Tm[(VMU doesn\325)37(t cause any side effects that the user is likely to notice.\))]TJ/F1 1 Tf11 0 0 11 90 305.304 Tm[(2.2.5 )-222(When a Controller is Removed and then Reconnected to the Same Port)]TJ/F11 1 Tf10 0 0 10 90 283.971 Tm(The following standards explain what to do when a controller is removed and then reconnected to the )TjT*(same port.)Tj/F18 1 Tf0 -2.7 TD(Recommended)Tj/F11 1 Tf0 -1.8 TD(If a controller is removed from a port that has been used and a compatible controller is reconnected to )Tj0 -1.2 TD(the same port, input must be resumed as soon as the second controller is connected.)Tj0 -1.8 TD-0.02 Tc(Reconnecting a different controller is permitted, as long as both controllers are Sega Dreamcast-compatible.)TjT*0 Tc[(If a controller is equipped with external memory)92(, both the controller and its external memory must be )]TJ0 -1.2 TD(recognized. \(Refer to Chapter 15, \323Backup.\323\))TjETendstreamendobj1146 0 obj<< /ProcSet [ /PDF /Text ] /Font << /F1 619 0 R /F11 441 0 R /F14 184 0 R /F18 731 0 R >> /ExtGState << /GS3 616 0 R >> >> endobj1147 0 obj<< /Type /Page /Parent 1187 0 R /Resources 1149 0 R /Contents 1148 0 R /CropBox [ 36 72 576 720 ] /B [ 1905 0 R ] >> endobj1148 0 obj<< /Length 2222 >> stream
